    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_28c6f156760871a0abbaaf8e3785ca203e33e4209e692e5cb4a780ac15107951",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The upper and lower bounds reach the same shift-dependent pairwise factor through different interfaces. The upper route logarithmizes the zeta product, controls weighted log-zeta level sets through a prime-polynomial covariance parameter W, and recovers the moment by layer-cake integration. The lower route correlates a smoothed coefficient expansion of the zeta product with a short resonator, uses Fourier localization to retain its diagonal, and evaluates that resonator norm through an Euler product and clustered residues.",
