    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_81ab9ccbe52856b2489c09c5df40cceffb825128262a702bdb872bde8912d639",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source handles coalescence by combining singular contributions before evaluating the limit. In the matrix model, a joint characteristic-polynomial moment becomes an ordinary moment of order 2k when N|alpha| tends to zero, while at finite scaled separation the apparently singular determinant/Vandermonde quotient has a confluent finite extension. In the zeta lower-bound norm, zero and all microscopic shifted poles are enclosed by one contour so their collective Laurent/Taylor contribution can be estimated without assigning unstable separate residues.",
